# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the smoke tiers: third-party code only.
#
# GLib's GMutex and GCond are raw futexes on Linux, invisible to TSan, so every
# handoff between GLib's own threads (pango's fontconfig loader, the GDBus
# worker, the GTask pool) looks like a race. These libraries are not
# instrumented: their frames only show up as the direct caller of an
# intercepted call (malloc, memcpy, close), never in the middle of a Waybar
# stack, so an entry matches only when the library made the access itself,
# allocated the memory or created the thread.
race:libglib-2.0.so.0
race:libgobject-2.0.so.0
race:libgio-2.0.so.0
race:libdconfsettings.so
race:libpangoft2-1.0.so.0
race:libfontconfig.so.1
